# What `gcloud builds submit` may leave out of the uploaded tarball.
#
# Without this every build shipped ~78 MB of rasters, archives and a QGIS
# project that no build step opens, and each tarball is kept in the Cloud
# Build bucket permanently: nine builds had already put 699 MB there, and one
# submit spent ten minutes uploading.
#
# Excluding a file a build needs would break the build, so this is a deny-list
# of things demonstrably unused rather than an allow-list.  Between them the
# three configs need: backend/, solver/, tools/, docs/data/segment_profiles.json
# (baked into the image for custom-pace requests) and docs/data/start_points.json
# (read by the start sweep).

.git
.gitignore
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Rasters, archives and GIS projects -- source data for building the network,
# never read at build time.
*.tif
*.tif.aux.xml
*.zip
*.qgz
*.qgz~
*.pdf

# Recorded tracks and superseded network snapshots.  The live network is
# lines_20250211 / points_20250211; the rest are history.
*_fkt*.geojson
eric_west_circuit.geojson
lines_20250109*.geojson
lines_20250117.geojson
lines_20250128*.geojson
points_20250109.geojson

# Published itineraries.  The image serves these from GitHub Pages, not from
# inside the container, and the preset batch regenerates them rather than
# reading them.
docs/data/preset_*.json
